          "source_text_sha256": "8e8ca13595792572407380f22930f1f9891d4891507632b77cf7e3603f744e45",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Summary: Observations of a bright point in the sky during foggy conditions; sensation of \"yawing\" of the PAN; likely astronomical misperception of Venus or the star Arcturus.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "623fee80584426140794bc6de562e44947eabd195e78ae7aab05b67849c6145c"
        },
        {
          "end_ms": null,
          "error": null,
          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-4451b77bf778112bad85e166",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-6591c9c26c5bd50a2c283871",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-6591c9c26c5bd50a2c283871",
          "source_text_sha256": "891ab91a72327460168567e67c82fbb34dd273de3fbffb1e01b1da078ba04c47",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 14, 2015, at 7:15 a.m., a witness and his wife observed, through fog, a bright point in the sky that seemed to \"waver\" and slightly increase in size. Only one testimony was collected. The report on a geographical map of the observation direction described by the witness indicates an azimuth of approximately 135° (Southeast) (see attached map). The sky map shows, in this direction, the planet Venus at 22° elevation (compared to 60° reported by the witness) and very bright (magnitude -3.6). The less bright star Arcturus (magnitude 0.15) is at azimuth 117° and elevation 51°. The phenomenon described by the witness has all the characteristics of a very bright star observed through light fog: the other stars are occluded, and the phenomenon appears slightly distorted. The impression that this light \"wavered\" is characteristic of the autokinetic illusion (see: Perception of the motion of a bright point in the sky). The GEIPAN classifies this case as B: probable observation of Venus or Arcturus.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "cb6f4fc17dee1fb4e5a3df0acccce6abf6413ae9eef297031e12f286e597ff4a"
        }
      ],
